description:
## What

Multipurpose-generation sibling to `SmimeMailboxValidated` (the renamed
`SmimeProfile`, post PKIX-jbvb.9.1). Per CA/B Forum S/MIME BR §7.1.2.3(f)
EKU rules and §7.1.6.1 reserved OIDs: Multipurpose certs assert policy
OID `2.23.140.1.5.1.2` and permit `emailProtection` plus additional EKU
values (for document-signing crossover).

## API shape

```rust
/// CA/Browser Forum S/MIME Baseline Requirements — Mailbox-validated
/// profile (Multipurpose generation).
///
/// Reference, not authoritative. See crate-level rustdoc.
///
/// Asserts policy OID `2.23.140.1.5.1.2` (§7.1.6.1 / Appendix A).
/// Permits additional EKU values beyond `emailProtection` per §7.1.2.3(f)
/// Multipurpose row.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub struct SmimeMailboxValidatedMultipurpose;

impl Profile for SmimeMailboxValidatedMultipurpose {
    fn id(&self) -> &'static str { "cabf.smime.mailbox.multipurpose" }
    fn version(&self) -> &'static str { "1.0.14" }
    fn policy(&self, now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        // Baseline of SmimeMailboxValidated, with:
        // - required_leaf_policy_oids: [2.23.140.1.5.1.2]
        // - EKU: still requires emailProtection, but does not constrain
        //   the EKU set to emailProtection-only (Strict has the stricter
        //   constraint; Multipurpose does not).
        // - same 825d cap, same SAN rules, same algs, same RSA min
    }
}

pub const fn smime_mailbox_multipurpose_policy(now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy { ... }
```

## Subject DN rule

Per §7.1.4.2.3 (Mailbox-validated table) Multipurpose column: same as
Strict — minimal DN, organizationName SHALL NOT, all tier-distinguishing
attributes SHALL NOT.

`required_leaf_subject_dn_attrs` stays `None` (no DN-attribute rule for
this tier). Same as `SmimeMailboxValidated`.

## OID constant

Add `CABF_SMIME_MAILBOX_VALIDATED_MULTIPURPOSE_POLICY` =
`ObjectIdentifier::new_unwrap("2.23.140.1.5.1.2")`.

## Test fixture

Modeled after zlint's `smime_mp1_mv_eff1.pem` if it exists; otherwise
generate `smime-mailbox-multipurpose-self-signed-365d.der` via
extension to `gen-smime-tier-fixtures.py`. Same self-signed-anchor
pattern as the other tier fixtures.

## Acceptance

- `SmimeMailboxValidatedMultipurpose` ships and impls `Profile`.
- `smime_mailbox_multipurpose_policy(now_unix)` free function alias.
- Reference-not-authoritative rustdoc disclaimer matches other types.
- `id()` returns `"cabf.smime.mailbox.multipurpose"`.
- `required_leaf_policy_oids` set to `[2.23.140.1.5.1.2]`.
- Test fixture cross-validates pass with this profile, fail with the
  Strict sibling (`SmimeMailboxValidated`).
- CHANGELOG entry under `[Unreleased]`.
- `divergences.md` updated.
- `cargo test -p pkix-profiles-cabf --all-features` passes.
- `cargo clippy ... -D warnings` clean.

## Blocks on

- **PKIX-jbvb.9.1** — Mailbox Strict rename must land first so this
  ships under the correct sibling name.

